---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Corrections Policy" description="Corrections Policy of Rozgar Raasta Pakistan — how we fix mistakes and how you can report them.">
	<section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
		<h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl">Corrections Policy</h1>
		<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: 26 November 2026</p>
		<div class="prose-rrp mt-6">
			<h2>We correct mistakes</h2>
			<p>We aim to be accurate, but mistakes happen. When we find an error — a wrong deadline, a changed fee, a broken link, a closed opportunity still shown as open — we correct it as soon as we can.</p>
			<h2>How corrections appear</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>Small fixes (typos, broken links) are corrected silently and the "Last verified" date is updated.</li>
				<li>Material corrections (a wrong deadline, eligibility or fee) are fixed and the article's "Last verified" date is updated so readers can see it was reviewed.</li>
				<li>If an opportunity has closed, we change its status to Closed rather than deleting it, so the record stays honest.</li>
			</ul>
			<h2>How to report an error</h2>
			<p>Found a mistake? <a href="/contact">Contact us</a> and choose "Correction to a listing or article". Please include the page link and what is wrong. We review every report.</p>
			<h2>Outdated listings</h2>
			<p>Opportunities change. If a listing is past its deadline, our system marks it Closed. If you see an open listing that has actually closed, please tell us — it helps every reader.</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
